    // car-textures, issue 571: (method 15 car-info-full) and (method 16
    // car-info-full) are landed with real bodies and compile clean under
    // (mi), but their own fresh decode still resolves two raw pointer-math
    // write sites (the damage-array #f clear in method 15, the part-texture
    // store in method 15's else branch) to a bare `(pointer int32)` cast
    // that goalc's typecheck rejects for a symbol/texture value ("For set!
    // memory, got a 'symbol'/'texture' when expecting an 'int'"); the
    // landed source overrides these two casts by hand to `(pointer
    // symbol)`/`(pointer texture)` (same idiom as goal_src/jakx/engine/
    // game/settings.gc:2522 and goal_src/jakx/engine/anim/joint.gc:1477),
    // but the decompiler's own default write-side inference (Env.cpp
    // deliberately skips auto-casting on SET!, only on read) has no
    // config-level lever this rung could safely derive: type_casts.jsonc
    // needs a precise atomic-op index that is not recoverable from the
    // asm_functions_by_name debug dump (asm-forced functions skip the
    // atomic-op pass entirely) and would need decompiler instrumentation
