    // find-first-containing-nav-mesh, still held. (method 7 net-enemy)
    // (relocate) calls fixup-relocated-link (goal_src/jakx/engine/util/
    // obj-list.gc), itself an unlanded stub with no defun or goal_src extern
    // anywhere, the same undeclared-symbol class find-first-containing-nav-
    // mesh was before this rung landed it; still held. The og:preserve-this
    // note at the top of goal_src/jakx/levels/common/net-enemy.gc covers
    // both plus method-70 below plus two new boot-only risks the landed
    // chain now surfaces (unfilled net-enemy-level slots for methods
    // 75/76/77/78 and process-nettable-method-26/31).
    "(method 84 net-enemy)",
    "(method 7 net-enemy)",
    // net-enemy: (method 70 net-enemy)'s own 'fatal-impact case dispatches
    // mem-buffer-method-32/40/41, three more of mem-buffer's own unfilled
    // methods (mem-buffer.gc lands only methods 10/11); mem-buffer-method-32
    // has no landed return type, so the compiler cannot pick a register
    // class for its result ("get_preferred_reg_class called on NullType").
    // Its own 'respawn case is unblocked by find-first-containing-nav-mesh
    // now, but the case form is one compiled function, so the method as a
    // whole still fails to compile on this unrelated blocker; still held,
    // the og:preserve-this note at the top of goal_src/jakx/levels/common/
    // net-enemy.gc covers it.
    "(method 70 net-enemy)",
    // net-enemy: (method 66 net-enemy)'s own type_casts.jsonc fix (needed to
    // resolve a *net-players* vtable dispatch at its second call site)
    // reaches back onto the first call site's own array-index expression,
    // degrading it to raw pointer arithmetic against a value still typed
    // object ("Cannot do math on a object" on (* arg0 4)); the landed
    // goal_src hand-touches this one spot with (the-as int arg0) to compile,
    // an og:preserve-this hand-touch the raw decode does not carry.
    "(method 66 net-enemy)",
    // football2 (rung 3): net-powerup-method-53 is a genuine zero-arg
    // :methods override on powercell-dispenser (net-powerup-h.gc declares
    // it "(net-powerup-method-53 () none)", no implicit this at all), the
    // same defect class as pov-camera's methods 56/58/59 and time-box-obs's
    // net-powerup-method-55: the decompiler's defmethod printer omits the
    // type-name second argument this shape needs, emitting
    // "(defmethod net-powerup-method-53 () #t (none))", which goalc rejects
    // ("Method type must be a symbol, got ()", tracked as issue 483, not
    // fixed here). Unlike pov-camera, football2 lands many other functions
    // this rung that still need offline-test's own compile pass to gate
    // them, so this is a function-level skip rather than a whole-file skip;
    // the landed goal_src supplies the explicit-type-name form (defmethod
    // net-powerup-method-53 powercell-dispenser () #t (none)), the same
    // shape already landed for vehicle-method-180, process-nettable-
    // method-28 and net-powerup-method-55, so (mi) links clean. Keyed by
    // the decompiler's own FunctionName::to_string() form for a METHOD
    // ("(method 53 powercell-dispenser)"), not the printed GOAL symbol
    // name; skip_compile_functions matches against Function::name(), which
    // for a method returns that form (decompiler/Function/Function.h),
    // confirmed by testing the bare symbol name first and finding it did
    // not suppress the error.
    "(method 53 powercell-dispenser)",
    // football2 (rung 3): (method 90 powercell-footie) declares two
    // lazily-computed "hand" sentinel locals as (the-as int #f), each
    // later assigned the manually-inlined process->handle idiom; no
    // type_casts entry reaches a compilable print (see the type_casts.
    // jsonc comment at this function for what was tried), so goalc
    // rejects the raw decompile's own "(the-as int #f)" once it is later
    // assigned a handle value. The landed goal_src hand-corrects both
    // bindings to (the-as handle #f), the correct sentinel form.
    "(method 90 powercell-footie)",
    // lobby-dma (issue 571 car-load path): lobby-dma-reserve-hook's raw decompile
    // assigns dma-buffer's pointer-typed end field from a bare (&- pointer uint)
    // subtraction; &- has no special-cased compiler form (unlike &+'s
    // compile_pointer_add in goalc/compiler/compilation/Atoms.cpp) so it returns
    // int, and every other &- callsite in the tree (gkernel.gc, gstring.gc) wraps
    // the result in an explicit (the pointer ...) / (the-as pointer ...) cast at
    // the assignment site; the landed goal_src carries that same cast and
    // compiles clean under (mi) (Successfully built all 683 targets), but
    // offline-test always compiles the decompiler's own fresh, uncast output
    // (test/offline/framework/execution.cpp's compile() uses data.output_with_
    // skips, never goal_src), so it fails this one function regardless.
    "lobby-dma-reserve-hook",
    // wvehicle (falcon-wheels rung, wheel-constants leg): (method 220
    // wvehicle)'s own fresh decompile prints one raw store address as
    // plain pointer arithmetic on a value typed vector ("(+ s5-1 28)"),
    // which goalc rejects ("Cannot do math on a vector"); every other
    // offset off the same local in this method's own body already goes
    // through "&+" (the compiler's own special-cased pointer-add form,
    // same class as lobby-dma-reserve-hook's &- case above), so the
    // landed goal_src spells this one op the same way. offline-test always
    // compiles the decompiler's own fresh, uncast output, so it fails this
    // one function regardless.
    "(method 220 wvehicle)",
    // wvehicle m64 remainder rung: (method 64 wvehicle)'s own fresh
    // decompile falls into raw local-vars fallback (same rb-debugger/
    // dirty-eyes class above: five "sllv v1, v1, r0" process->handle
    // reinterpretations the decoder cannot render as the real macro), and
    // in that fallback mode the arg0-typed-object parameter is assigned
    // straight into wvehicle's rigid-body-vehicle-constants-typed `info`
    // field with no cast at all ("(set! (-> a0-0 info) a1-0)"), which
    // goalc rejects. The landed goal_src carries the real handle->process
    // macro at every sllv site and casts arg0 explicitly for the info
    // write and everywhere else it needs the narrower type. offline-test
    // always compiles the decompiler's own fresh, uncast output, so it
    // fails this one function regardless.
    "(method 64 wvehicle)",
    // default-menu, issue 571's UX successor (R3 of the debug-menu scoping
    // plan): all-texture-tweak-adjust's fresh decompile reads a literal
    // PLACEHOLDER token off a dynamic-array-field-access call, which is not
    // valid GOAL; the landed goal_src stubs it to (none) instead, matching
    // jak3's own precedent for the same function.
    "all-texture-tweak-adjust",
    // default-menu: dm-vu1-user-all-pick-func's fresh decompile carries a
    // bare label reference (L6899, "Failed to guess label use") for a static
    // 64-bit constant load/store at a raw offset; the landed goal_src
    // resolves it to a clean named-field idiom (matching the file's own
    // clean sibling dm-vu1-user-none-pick-func) with the constant read
    // directly off the object's own static data.
    "dm-vu1-user-all-pick-func",
    // default-menu: build-instance-list's fresh decompile carries four bare
    // label references (L859, L858, L857, L856) for its four (sort ...)
    // comparators; the landed goal_src hand-writes all four verbatim from
    // jak3's own landed twin (identical comparator repeated four times).
    "build-instance-list",
    // default-menu: debug-menu-make-camera-menu's fresh decompile carries a
    // bare label reference (L810) for the "Edit" '*cam-layout* toggle
    // callback; the landed goal_src hand-writes it verbatim from jak3's own
    // landed twin (cam-layout-start/cam-layout-stop, both already landed in
    // engine/camera/cam-layout.gc).
    "debug-menu-make-camera-menu",
    // default-menu: debug-menu-make-shader-menu's fresh decompile carries the
    // 17 int shader-tweak bare label references (L790..L630) plus the float
    // "tweak" field's own (L802), all resolved verbatim in landed goal_src
    // from jak3's own twin (gs-tex0/gs-tex1/gs-clamp share an identical bit
    // layout across games); confirmed by the offline suite's own compile
    // step, which fails on the first of these (L802) before this entry was
    // added.
    "debug-menu-make-shader-menu",
    // default-menu: debug-menu-context-make-default-menus's fresh decompile
    // still carries eight bare label references after this rung's own
    // hacks.jsonc pair_functions_by_name fix (which clears the function's
    // register-pairing errors, not this separate bare-label-lambda defect):
    // two resolve verbatim from jak3 (Traffic Start/Kill, L389/L387); the
    // other six are held (Kill Target/Hit Target/Save Continue depend on
    // *target*, a symbol that does not exist anywhere in jakx; Get All
    // Vehicles Parts/Get All Tasks/Trick Out Vehicles are jakx-only with no
    // jak3 twin and zero recovered body). See goal_src for the per-site
    // og:preserve-this notes.
    "debug-menu-context-make-default-menus",
    // default-menu: eight named functions fail decode entirely into
    // register-soup (hundreds of local-vars, "Failed to guess stack use")
    // rather than a resolvable bare label; the landed goal_src holds each as
    // a type-correct trivial stub (see the per-function og:preserve-this
    // notes in goal_src for the specific error and, for the two
    // *anim-tester*-dependent ones, the offset mismatch against jak3's own
    // landed anim-tester type that rules out a same-offset port).
    "dm-cam-settings-func",
    "dm-cam-setting-float",
    "dm-subdiv-int",
    "dm-current-continue",
    "build-shader-list",
    "dm-split-screen-toggle-pick-func",
    "dm-anim-tester-flag-func",
    "dm-anim-tester-func"
  ],
  "skip_compile_states": {
    // bad handle->process folds (jak3 carries the same class of entries); the
    // landed goal_src carries hand-folded handle->process at these sites
    "(idle manipy)": ["event", "code"],
    // kras-obs: (defstate idle (kras-fireworks-ship-a) ...)'s :exit and :post
    // handlers both decode as raw label references (L122, L114); goal_src
    // carries the full analysis for the other three handlers.
    "(idle kras-fireworks-ship-a)": ["exit", "post"],
    // kras-obs: (defstate idle (kras-flag) ...)'s :code handler decodes as a
    // raw label reference (L107); goal_src carries the full analysis for the
    // other four handlers.
    "(idle kras-flag)": ["code"],
    // desarena-obs: (defstate idle (palm-tree) ...)'s :event handler decodes as
    // a raw label reference (L39); goal_src carries the full analysis for the
    // other four handlers.
    "(idle palm-tree)": ["event"],
    // desarena-obs: (defstate vibrate (palm-tree) ...)'s :event handler also
    // decodes as a raw label reference (L31); goal_src carries the full
    // analysis for the other four handlers.
    "(vibrate palm-tree)": ["event"],
    // train-obs: (defstate idle (train-car) :virtual #t ...)'s :event handler
    // decodes a manual find-parent-method fallback whose result the compiler
    // types as plain `function`, which has no `event` field to read; goal_src
    // carries the full analysis for the other (inherited) :post handler.
    "(idle train-car)": ["event"],
    // train-obs: (defstate idle (train) :virtual #t ...)'s :post handler
    // decodes as a raw label reference (L10); goal_src carries the full
    // analysis for the other four handlers.
    "(idle train)": ["post"],
    // kras-obs: (defstate idle (kras-windsock) ...)'s :code handler decodes as
    // a raw label reference (L100); goal_src carries the full analysis for the
    // other four handlers.
    "(idle kras-windsock)": ["code"],
    // title-obs: (defstate target-title (target) ...)'s :enter handler decodes
    // as a raw label reference (L40); goal_src carries the full analysis for
    // the other three handlers.
    // peak-obs: (defstate idle (peak-snowball) :virtual #t ...)'s :post
    // handler fails the same matrix-copy! typecheck as (method 17
    // peak-snowball) above (the decoded arg1 casts through quaternion instead
    // of matrix); goal_src carries the full analysis.
    "(idle peak-snowball)": ["post"],
    // kras-obs: (defstate idle (kras-pump-break) :virtual #t ...)'s :event
    // handler fails the same NullType reg-class failure as peak-obs's own
    // (method 80 peak-snowball) above, on the same
    // process-nettable-method-27/-29 pair; goal_src carries the full analysis.
    "(idle kras-pump-break)": ["event"],
    // kras-obs: (defstate explode (kras-pump-break-draw) ...)'s :event handler
    // decodes as a raw label reference (L11), and its :enter handler does
    // pointer arithmetic on a collide-shape-prim-typed value ((+ v1-9 108)
    // feeding s.w!) the compiler rejects; goal_src carries the full analysis
    // for the other handlers.
    "(explode kras-pump-break-draw)": ["event", "enter"],
    // vehicle-states (vehicle band): (defstate player-control (vehicle)
    // ...)'s :enter handler decodes as a raw label reference (L28), an
    // anon-function the decompiler never recognized as a proper function; the
    // raw handler also carries the eight-byte read at self+460 (spanning two
    // fields, no cast expresses it) and the sllv reinterpretation pseudo-op
    // the wvehicle-small-tier rung held. Both held issues live inside this
    // one unresolved body; goal_src omits the key entirely (credits-obs
    // precedent) and carries the full analysis for the state's other
    // handlers.
    "(player-control vehicle)": ["enter"],
    // visvol-edit: (defstate idle (visvol-editor) :virtual #t ...)'s :trans
    // handler decodes self->proc's handle->process deref as the raw
    // .asm.sllv.r0 / pid-check triple (the same class "(idle manipy)" above
    // holds); goal_src hand-folds it to (handle->process ...) and carries the
    // full analysis for the state's other three handlers.
    "(idle visvol-editor)": ["trans"],
    // wvehicle-states: (defstate explode (wvehicle) :virtual #t ...)'s :enter
    // handler decodes as explosion-init-params being built cleanly (both
    // handle fields, the stack struct) up to the same sllv reinterpretation
    // pseudo-op "(player-control vehicle)" above holds, this time on a
    // ppointer-chase result rather than a directly-loaded handle field;
    // parked as asm by config (decompiler/config/jakx/ntsc_v1/hacks.jsonc,
    // "(anon-function 18 wvehicle-states)"); goal_src omits the key entirely
    // (credits-obs precedent) and carries the full analysis for :post.
    "(explode wvehicle)": ["enter"],
    // wvehicle-states: (defstate explode-into-nothing (wvehicle) :virtual #t
    // ...)'s :enter handler is the same class as "(explode wvehicle)" above
    // (asm-parked as "(anon-function 16 wvehicle-states)"); goal_src omits
    // the key entirely and carries the full analysis for :code/:post.
    "(explode-into-nothing wvehicle)": ["enter"],
    // net-enemy: (defstate in-ragdoll (net-enemy) :virtual #t ...)'s :event
    // and :enter handlers both decode as raw label references (L92, L126);
    // :enter's own body run-function-in-process's ragdoll-proc-init-by-
    // other, an active extern with no defun anywhere in goal_src, and
    // :event's own handle-deref sequence against ragdoll-proc sits inside a
    // CFG the decompiler could not fold into a real behavior form either.
    // goal_src omits both keys entirely (credits-obs precedent) and carries
    // the full analysis for :exit/:trans/:code.
    "(in-ragdoll net-enemy)": ["event", "enter"],
    // target (scene chain, #522): (defstate target-float (target) ...)'s
    // :enter and :trans handlers both decode as raw label references (L8,
    // L1); landing target-nearest-dist in the same object is what first
    // brings "target" into the REF corpus, surfacing this pre-existing gap
    // (this state was never landed and goal_src carries none of it yet).
    // :event, :exit and :code/:post all resolve to real forms already.
    "(target-float target)": ["enter", "trans"]
  }
}